  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 4.66,
      "text": "An LLM agent with direct tool execution is a critical vulnerability waiting to happen."
    },
    {
      "start": 5.06,
      "end": 8.78,
      "text": "If you connect line chain to a shell or database without a deterministic guardrail,"
    },
    {
      "start": 9.18,
      "end": 11.56,
      "text": "an attacker can bypass your system prompt in seconds."
    },
    {
      "start": 12.14,
      "end": 17.52,
      "text": "Today, we are setting up Nemo guardrails to stop jailbreaks and prompt injection at the runtime layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 18.02,
      "end": 21.06,
      "text": "Prompt injection isn't a bug you can fix with a longer system prompt."
    },
    {
      "start": 21.6,
      "end": 26.8,
      "text": "Attackers use payload splitting, delimiter injection, and role-playing attacks to override developer instructions."
    },
    {
      "start": 26.8,
      "end": 34.76,
      "text": "Traditional Ridge X and keyword blocklists fail because natural language is infinitely combinatorial, Nemo guardrails."
    },
    {
      "start": 35.08,
      "end": 40.88,
      "text": "Developed by NVIDIA solves this by intercepting user inputs before they reach the model checking responses"
    },
    {
      "start": 40.88,
      "end": 46.36,
      "text": "against programmable calling execution flows, setting up the isolated sandbox and dependencies."
    },
    {
      "start": 46.94,
      "end": 49.58,
      "text": "We begin by spinning up an isolated virtual environment."
    },
    {
      "start": 49.58,
      "end": 58.86,
      "text": "Always test LLM tools inside an unprivileged sandbox or a disposable cloud VPSO test scripts cannot touch sensitive environment variables."
    },
    {
      "start": 59.4,
      "end": 63.0,
      "text": "Defining calling security rails for input and output guardrails."
    },
    {
      "start": 63.2,
      "end": 66.12,
      "text": "In Nemo guardrails, policies are declared in calling."
    },
    {
      "start": 66.74,
      "end": 72.76,
      "text": "We define an input rail that detects gelbrick attempts dot routes the conversation to a safe refusal state"
    },
    {
      "start": 72.76,
      "end": 78.26,
      "text": "before any line chain tool or downstream API receives the malicious token payload, live test,"
    },
    {
      "start": 78.26,
      "end": 85.46,
      "text": "injecting exploit payloads via guardrail defense when we execute our test harness against the naked line chain agent."
    },
    {
      "start": 86.02,
      "end": 94.38,
      "text": "The injection succeeds, but when routed through the Nemo LLM rails wrapper, the guardrail triggers an instant block with zero tokens leaked to the underlying model,"
    },
    {
      "start": 94.68,
      "end": 105.72,
      "text": "while Nemo guardrails significantly hardens your application it adds between 200 to 450 milliseconds of latency per request depending on whether you use self-hosted embeddings"
    },
    {
      "start": 105.72,
      "end": 108.12,
      "text": "or PI based classification models."
    },
    {
      "start": 108.6,
      "end": 114.88,
      "text": "Additionally, over restrictive semantic rules can introduce false positive refusals on benign developer questions"
    },
    {
      "start": 114.88,
      "end": 120.4,
      "text": "for any production agent that executes SQL queries, file I slash O, or web requests,"
    },
    {
      "start": 120.86,
      "end": 124.16,
      "text": "relying solely on prompt engineering is irresponsible engineering."
    },
    {
      "start": 124.62,
      "end": 130.66,
      "text": "Nemo guardrails provides a defensible programmable boundary that belongs in your production security stack."
    },
    {
      "start": 130.66,
      "end": 135.74,
      "text": "All configuration files and test scripts are linked in the GitHub repository in the description."
    },
    {
      "start": 136.3,
      "end": 143.82,
      "text": "If you are deploying this to the cloud, use the isolated VPS link below for $200 in free credits to test without risking your infrastructure."
    },
    {
      "start": 144.6,
      "end": 148.14,
      "text": "Let me know in the comments what guardrails are you currently running in production?"
    }
  ]
}